  "title": "export a walker, import in main",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "md": "## Two files\n\n`walker.mjs` exports `walkLength`. `main.mjs` imports it and prints `2` for `[\"east\", \"south\"]`."
    },
    {
      "type": "predict",
      "id": "export-name",
      "promptMd": "`export function walkLength` is…",
      "kind": "mcq",
      "choices": [
        {
          "id": "global",
          "md": "A global in every file automatically"
        },
        {
          "id": "named",
          "md": "A named export you must import"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "named"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "id": "two-files",
      "engine": "javascript",
      "entry": "main.mjs",
      "promptMd": "> Export from `walker.mjs`, import in `main.mjs`, print `2`.",
      "files": [
        {
          "path": "files/walker.mjs",
          "role": "edit"
        },
        {
          "path": "files/main.mjs",
          "role": "edit"
        },
        {
          "path": "files/hidden.test.mjs",
          "role": "hidden-test"
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "stdout",
          "equals": "2"
        },
        {
          "type": "js-assert"
        }
      ],
      "hintLadder": [
        {
          "level": 1,
          "kind": "concept",
          "md": "import { walkLength } from \"./walker.mjs\""
        },
        {
          "level": 4,
          "kind": "assist",
          "md": "walker.mjs: export function walkLength(dirs) { return dirs.length }\nmain.mjs: import { walkLength } from \"./walker.mjs\"\nconsole.log(walkLength([\"east\", \"south\"]))"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "description": "Export a walker from one file and import it in another."
